ADREPORT(a) should work, but it probably doesn't show up by default. I think you need to summary(rep,"report") as in https://search.r-project.org/CRAN/refmans/TMB/html/summary.sdreport.html

A bigger concern is the interpretation of uncertainties of ADREPORTed random effects. Normally, sdreport will apply a generalized delta method, see:
https://search.r-project.org/CRAN/refmans/TMB/html/sdreport.html
However, your manual implementation will only provide the second term (J*V(theta)*t(J)) representing the standard delta method applied on the random effect modes. I don't have an easy workaround to give the full uncertainty.

